HARDWARE INTERFACES

The GPU driver programs a documented device, and the register offsets, class
method numbers and bring-up sequences it uses are facts about that hardware,
learned by reading published open-source drivers: nouveau in the Linux kernel
(GPL-2.0-only), Mesa's NIL and NVK (MIT), and NVIDIA's open-gpu-kernel-modules
(MIT/GPL-2.0 dual). The owning modules name their source in place — see
src/drivers/gpu/display/modeset.zig, src/drivers/gl/ada/til.zig and
src/drivers/gpu/gsp/gsp.zig. The implementations here are original Zig written
against those interfaces; no code was copied from them.
